.TH MOUNTBRIDGE 1 "September 2026" "mountbridge 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mountbridge \- network mount manager for NFS, SMB/CIFS and SSHFS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mountbridge
.RB [ \-\-hidden ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mountbridge
is a GTK3 application for managing network mounts. Mount definitions are
stored in
.IR ~/.config/mountbridge/mounts.json ;
passwords are kept in the system keyring (Secret Service).
.PP
SSHFS mounts run as the user, at the configured local path (by default
.IR ~/.mounts/<name> ).
NFS and SMB/CIFS mounts are made by the root helper
.I /usr/libexec/mountbridge/mountbridge\-helper
at
.IR /mnt/mountbridge/<user>/<name> ,
with a shortcut at the configured local path. The helper allows only
nfs, nfs4 and cifs, only allow-listed mount options, and always adds
.BR nosuid , nodev .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-hidden
Start minimised to the system tray.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH NFS/SMB ACCESS
Members of the
.B mountbridge
group may run the helper through
.BR sudo (8),
as configured in
.IR /etc/sudoers.d/mountbridge .
To give a user access:
.PP
.RS
.B adduser
.I user
.B mountbridge
.RE
.PP
The change takes effect at the user's next login.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mountbridge/mounts.json
Mount definitions.
.TP
.I /etc/sudoers.d/mountbridge
Grants the mountbridge group use of the root helper.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mount.nfs (8),
.BR mount.cifs (8),
.BR sshfs (1),
.BR sudoers (5)
